      "approx_t": 4,
      "text": "Almost everyone points at the nose. The nose isn't what changed. The chin is."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 9,
      "text": "Your eye reads a feature against everything around it."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 13,
      "text": "This is every pixel that changed. Almost none of them are on the nose."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 17,
      "text": "It didn't shrink. The face caught up."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 20,
      "text": "One. The nose and the chin are read as one."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 24,
      "text": "A chin that sits back leaves the nose out in front."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 29,
      "text": "Bring the chin forward and the nose settles back. Same nose. Every time."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 34,
      "text": "Two. Another face. The lid and the eye."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 39,
      "text": "Skin resting on the lashes closes the eye beneath it."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 43,
      "text": "Lift the hood and the eye reads open. The eye didn't grow. The cover moved."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 51,
      "text": "Three. A face is read in thirds."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 54,
      "text": "Hairline to brow. Brow to nose. Nose to chin."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 57,
      "text": "Move one boundary and all three change."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 62.0,
      "text": "None of this tells you what to do. It tells you why one feature can't answer it."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 67.0,
      "text": "Faces are read whole. Not feature by feature."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 71.0,
      "text": "Push your lower jaw forward a few millimetres. Hold it."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 76.0,
      "text": "Now look at your nose. Watch your nose get smaller. You didn't touch your nose."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 80.0,
      "text": "So the question was never one feature. It's what the whole face does when it moves."
    },
    {
